name 'self-paced-TCaAI-L1-ComputationalThinkingCFU'
title 'Check for Understanding'
description 'Match each example with their computational thinking practice.'
height'150'
width'600'


question 'Jordan is testing an AI image generator and says, "Instead of changing everything at once, I\’m only going to adjust the style of the prompt first so I can see exactly what effect that has on the image."'
answer 'Algorithmic Thinking'

question 'Samira notices that every time she asks AI to generate a “healthy meal,” it produces similar foods and presentation styles. She begins identifying repeated assumptions across multiple outputs.'
answer 'Pattern Recognition'

question 'Luis is reviewing an AI-generated response and says, "I\’m going to ignore the wording for now and just focus on whether the information itself seems accurate and trustworthy."'
answer 'Abstraction'

question 'Taylor is trying to figure out why an AI chatbot gave an incorrect answer. She says, "Let\’s break this down into smaller parts: what was the prompt, what information did the AI use, and where did the response go wrong?"'
answer 'Decomposition'


